{"id":"G2012","lemma":"ἐπίτροπος","transliteration":"epitropos","sayIt":"epitropos","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, masculine","gloss":"manager","meaning":"ἐπίτροπος, -ου, ὁ\n(ἐπιτρέπω), [in LXX: 2Ma.11:1 2Mac 13:2 2Mac 14:2 * ;]\n1. an administrator, a steward: Mat.20:3, Luk.8:3.\n2. a guardian (with genitive of person(s), 2Mac, ll. with): Gal.4:2.†\n(AS)","glosses":["foreman","household manager","guardians"],"count":3,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"mat-20","v":8,"renderings":{"bsb":"foreman","kjv":"steward"}},{"chapterId":"luk-8","v":3,"renderings":{"bsb":"household manager","kjv":"steward"}},{"chapterId":"gal-4","v":2,"renderings":{"bsb":"guardians","kjv":"tutors"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Matthew 20:8","note":"When evening had come, the lord of the vineyard said to his manager, ‘Call the laborers and pay them their wages, beginning from the last to the first.’","source":"web"},{"ref":"Luke 8:3","note":"and Joanna, the wife of Chuzas, Herod’s steward; Susanna; and many others; who served them from their possessions.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Galatians 4:2","note":"but is under guardians and stewards until the day appointed by the father.","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20120","lemma":"ἀποσκοπέω","transliteration":"aposkopeō","gloss":"to regard"},{"id":"G20121","lemma":"ἀποσκορπίζω","transliteration":"aposkorpizō","gloss":"to scatter widely"},{"id":"G20122","lemma":"ἀποσκυθίζω","transliteration":"aposkuthizō","gloss":"be shaved bare"},{"id":"G20123","lemma":"ἀποστρεβαλόομαι","transliteration":"apostrebaloomai","gloss":"be tortured"},{"id":"G20124","lemma":"ἀποσφενδονάω","transliteration":"aposphendonaō","gloss":"to hurl"},{"id":"G20125","lemma":"ἀποτεκνόομαι","transliteration":"apoteknoomai","gloss":"be childless"},{"id":"G20126","lemma":"ἀποτίναγμα","transliteration":"apotinagma","gloss":"tow"},{"id":"G20127","lemma":"ἀποτίνυμι","transliteration":"apotinumi","gloss":"to repay"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGN